WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.230
And again!

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.230
God Rage!

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.780
Hey, get a hold of yourself, Kaito! Kaito!

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.240
Kaito!!

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.720
Faker-<i>sama</i>... Dr. Faker-<i>sama</i>!

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.230
Kaito... <i>That</i> Kaito has lost to Tron!

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.460
After all that happened, shouldn't we terminate the tournament...

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.210
Why should we terminate it now?

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.750
Everything goes as planned.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.100
As long as we still have the Sphere Field to go,

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.430
the Finals will continue as planned.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.210
As-As you wish.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.040
Kaito... has lost...

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.260
Kaito's... Kaito's soul is...

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.140
Tron took it away.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.210
The only thing Kaito wanted... was to save Haruto.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.520
He only wanted to protect what's precious to him.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:13.320
Yuma.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:20.100
Tron used the power of the crest to take away the souls of Droite, Kaito, and Haruto.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.580
If he is defeated in a Duel...

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.350
If that power were to be destroyed, then perhaps...

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:29.540
Sure, I'll do that! I'm gonna kick his butt for sure!

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.560
Yuma!

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:31.730
Yuma!
Guys...

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:34.840
Good luck to you, Yuma-<i>kun</i>.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.370
I've got high hopes for you!

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.680
Sure, leave it to me!

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.420
I'll show you the power of my 'Bring it to 'Em'!

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.600
You better get the championship<i>~meow</i>.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.770
Yuma, you're representing us as a Duelist.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.100
Don't you let yourself be defeated by that Tron!

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.670
Come on, Yuma, you as well!

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:55.460
Yuma!
 Yuma-<i>kun</i>.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.420
Y-Yeah!

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.060
Guys, thank you. I'm gonna win the championship for sure.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.000
With everyone's feelings.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.400
Yeah!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.370
Yuma!

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.540
Wow, a Duel Lunch!

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.740
Thank you, Kotori!

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.500
Eat it and be sure to win!

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:32.510
Leave it to me!

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:35.170
You better promise me, okay?

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.880
I'm absolutely positive!

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.360
Now then, I'm going.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.970
He'd still go even if I stopped him...

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:54.880
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:02:55.170 --> 00:03:00.220
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:17.070
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.870
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.460
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:33.500
<i>It's too soon for us to turn back now</i>

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:38.590
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:44.140
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:49.940
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.980
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:03:55.530 --> 00:04:00.450
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:06.120
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.290
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:18.380
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.740
Like there is only one sun in the sky, this shining glory is just as unique!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.120
Anyone who dared to stand in their way was deemed a foe.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.960
Many a battle did they fight, including the survival-death matches,

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:36.250
"Number 65: An All-Out Battle Between Numbers! Yuma vs Tron!
 The Surprising Duel in the Ultra Different Dimension!"

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.040
<i>during the first part of the World Duel Carnivals.</i>

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.340
<i>They defeated enemy after enemy to get here.</i>

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:44.090
<i>Whom will shine the sun on their dash to immense glory?</i>

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.760
<i>These two have survived this far!</i>

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.970
<i>I give you the Dark Horse of the tournament, the Duelist with the mysterious mask, Tron!</i>

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:58.270
<i>Against the miraculous wonder boy, Yuma Tsukumo!</i>

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.780
Yuma, do your best!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.450
<i>The Final of the century!</i>

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.910
<i>And the stage now will be changed.</i>

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:10.280
<i>Made by Heartland's top advanced technology:</i>

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.620
<i>The Sphere Field!</i>

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:18.710
That Sphere Field is a far cry from any of the fields you've fought on up until now.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.130
It is simulated space from the Parallel Worlds.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.800
Tron, Yuma...

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.220
Use all the Numbers you have to your heart's content.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.600
Regardless of the outcome, you both will...

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.030
Wha... What is that?!

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.670
So this is the Sphere Field.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.340
Just what is this thing?

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.390
So that Faker managed to complete it.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.980
Now, Sphere Field, take our two best Duelists...

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.020
<i>...to the sky!</i>

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.270
What's the deal with that field?

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:26.820
To summarize, that means this special field is built by a mysterious energy from a different dimension.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.740
Good job making it this far!

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.740
Tron, you...!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:38.580
While I was wandering the threshold between the Parallel World in a living Hell...

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.630
I gave up on life countless times.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:48.470
In those moments, I recalled the memory of your father, Kazuma, who gave me constant support.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.470
He used to say this quite often:

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.730
"Friends, companions, and a heart that will never give up."

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:02.690
But after being betrayed by Faker, I came to understand.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.070
His talk about friends and comrades...

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.860
...all became completely meaningless to me!

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.830
But I have to admit that the part about, "a heart that will never give up" is quite important.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:20.210
It was because I never gave up that I had the hope to get my revenge.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.040
And I was able to be reborn in this form!

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.000
That's not right! And I promised III!

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.380
He asked me: "Please save my family!"

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:36.260
Tron, this is why I'll fight for III with everything I've got!

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.890
And I'll save you!

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.350
To <i>save</i> me? From <i>what</i>, exactly?

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.310
Isn't that obvious?!

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.520
I will drive out the demon of revenge inside you!

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:52.410
For your revenge, you sacrificed III, V, and IV!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:56.240
But in the end, those kids haven't been very useful.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:01.290
As punishment, they are now lying side by side as three hollow shells without souls.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:03.580
Hollow shells?

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.960
Right. The crest I gave the three of them

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:12.220
granted them power, but as a price, it was directly linked to their souls.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.340
Numbers require a huge amount of power.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:18.010
If such a Duel is lost, the soul will be consumed.

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.310
The result is quite obvious, isn't it?

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.100
You... knew that this would happen...?!

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.520
Can a human with such an evil heart truly exist?

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.440
And you call yourself their parent!?

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:34.820
They already knew about your emptiness of revenge, but you...

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.660
Isn't that the bond between parent and child?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:41.450
I mean, <i>Faker</i> is the one to blame for all this!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.710
Why won't you get revenge against him?

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.920
Dr. Faker did take Kazuma away from you, you know.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:51.210
My Dad... My dad would never want me to take revenge!

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:52.340
Really?

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.510
I wonder if Kazuma really thinks that.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.640
No, couldn't it be that he already started his revenge?

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.680
Isn't that right, Astral?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.480
What are you trying to say?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.480
A terrible power is dwelling in the Numbers.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.980
They could destroy this world with their enormous force, couldn't they?

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:19.530
If so, aren't you the messenger lending him power to take revenge on this world?

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.540
Kazuma did send Astral to this world, didn't he?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.710
That can't... Astral is the messenger to take revenge on this world?

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:33.880
Aren't you collecting this terrible power as well, Faker!?

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.600
<i>- What the?
 - Who's that old guy?</i>

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:44.230
- He's kinda scary!
 - Is he about to do something?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.480
That's Dr. Faker?

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.650
<i>Long time no see, Byron.</i>

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.070
<i>Your rejuvenation took me by surprise.</i>

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.070
It's all thanks to you.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.410
I'll go pay you a visit in due time.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.950
As soon as I take all of Yuma's Numbers, that is.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.160
Stop joking around here! Dr. Faker! Tron!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:07.580
I'll take care of you no-good adults once and for all!

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.460
<i>Now </i>that<i> sounds interesting. I'm looking <i>forward</i> to it.</i>

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.590
I'll show you! We're gonna win this, Astral!

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.310
<i>Now, for everyone here,</i>

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.850
<i>allow me to explain the Dueling rules of the Sphere Field!</i>

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:34.320
<i>This field has been developed to maximize the power of the Numbers.</i>

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:39.780
<i>Each player can overlay two Monsters of the same level in his hand,</i>

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:46.870
<i>then, ignoring the Summoning conditions, a random Numbers Monster will be Special Summoned from the Extra Deck!</i>

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.210
<i>But a Number that has been Summoned in that way</i>

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:54.300
<i>will be destroyed once its Overlay Units are used up!</i>

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.340
<i>Now, use this as best as you can.</i>

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:00.630
<i>The Duelists chosen by the Numbers!</i>

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.260
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.850
Right, let's go!

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:15.860
Duel!!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:21.360
I will start! My turn! Draw!

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.870
I'll use the effect of the field right from the start!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.410
I will take 2 Level Four Monsters from my hand.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:32.540
I Overlay Heraldic Beasts Aberconway and Yale!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.420
There's a Number coming already?!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:40.090
Of course, it's a Number I can't choose myself.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.850
I Special Summon Number 56,

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.600
Goldrat in Defense Position!

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.780
With this, I end my turn.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.780
600 Defense Points? A Number this weak...

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:03.910
Yuma.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:04.700
Huh?

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:09.830
Do you think the Numbers really have the power to destroy the world?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:11.540
Astral.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.000
Don't tell me you're still thinking about what Tron said.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.040
I don't have any memories.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.550
Have I really been sent to this world for revenge?

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.430
Astral...

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.140
I don't have a clue why you've been sent to this world.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.850
But I've come to know more than anyone that you're not a bad guy.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.730
But if the Numbers really have that crazy sort of power,

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.650
these guys should never get a hold of them!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.110
Astral, I'll hand them to you because I know you'll do the right thing with them.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.160
I believe in you.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.710
Yuma, I understand.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:57.960
Let's do our best to defeat this Tron.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:58.880
Sure!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:03.880
How about we surprise him with some secret strategy you've been saving up 'til now?

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:05.630
I don't have one.

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.220
Oh? Wait!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.680
You shouldn't rely on me anymore today!

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:15.440
By the way, about strategy and your Dueling style...

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.940
We're back to our usual way now!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.270
That's what I'm talking about!

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.070
Let's go! My turn! Draw!

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.740
Yes, it's there! I'll bring it to 'em!

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:33.080
From my hand, I Overlay the Level Four Gagaga Magician and Gogogo Golem!

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.170
This is the Number I Summon!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.090
Come forth, Number 12!

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:49.890
Armor Ninja Crimson Shadow!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.180
That's a good draw!

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:59.100
To summarize, with his Attack Power, he can defeat Goldrat!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.020
Force yourself through!

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.780
Go, Yuma!

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:06.150
Crimson Shadow, attack Goldrat!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.990
Crimson Slash of Moon Shadow!

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.200
Good!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.790
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:26.510
My turn! Draw!

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:31.180
<i>Nice work, Yuma, Astral... That's the way!</i>

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.720
<i>Bring forth more of your power.</i>

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.350
<i>The more power you bring forth,</i>

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.560
<i>...the tighter you grasp your own necks!</i>

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.860
I'll take two Level Four Monsters from my hand!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:49.740
I Overlay Heraldic Beasts Twin Head Eagle and Aberconway!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.120
Come forth, Number 10!

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.500
Shining White Knight Illuminator!

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.510
Tha... That's... Kaito's Number.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:09.840
Oh? So Kaito used this, did he?

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:12.470
I guess he's useful for <i>something</i> after <i>all</i>!

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.600
Tron... You bastard!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.470
Don't be swayed by his words!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:21.350
I detach one Overlay Unit from Illuminator,

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:24.150
to send one card from my hand to the Graveyard.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.030
And I draw one card from the deck.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.150
And then I...

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:35.700
...activate the effect of Aberconway, who was sent to the Graveyard as an Overlay Unit.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.750
By Banishing Aberconway from my Graveyard,

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.670
I can add the other Aberconway in my Graveyard back into my hand.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:44.710
He's going for it again?!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:49.840
I Overlay the Level Four Heraldic Beasts Aberconway and Leo!

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:55.300
Come forth, Number 30!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.930
Acid Golem of Destruction!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.690
He's got... two Numbers now?

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.150
And there's still another one.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.440
Yuma-<i>kun</i>, this is my <i>special service</i> to you!

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:14.870
I Overlay two Heraldic Beast Unicorns!

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:19.700
Come forth, Number 8!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.760
Heraldic King Genome Heriter!

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.890
So you showed yourself, Genome Heriter...

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.100
He's got three Numbers now?!

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.430
You're aware, aren't you, Yuma?

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.770
Genome Heriter has many Monster Effects.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.780
Now, let's go! I'll activate Genome Heriter's effect!

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:55.450
By detaching one Overlay Unit, for this turn,

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:59.990
the Attack Power of one battling Monster the opponent controls will become zero!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:07.210
Now Crimson Shadow's Attack Power changes to zero!

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:13.090
Then Genome Heriter's Attack Power becomes the original Attack Power of my opponent's Monster it battles!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.840
Though, the Attack Power didn't change at all.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.890
Oh crap!

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:19.720
It's coming!

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.430
Genome Heriter, give the death blow to Crimson Shadow!

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.190
I'll just use Crimson Shadow's effect!

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.100
Wait, Yuma!

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:29.270
Use the Trap.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:33.150
If you just answer the attack with a Monster Effect, we'll still receive damage.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:36.660
If we take consecutive attacks like this, we will...

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:38.160
Understood.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:40.950
Trap, activate! Half Guard!

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.160
Half Guard negates destruction during this battle,

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.080
and after the battle, Crimson Shadow will change into Defense Position.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.430
Darn... he took a lot Life from me!

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.100
Tch... So it's in Defense Mode now, is it?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:13.150
Well, never mind that. Go, Acid Golem!

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:15.570
Acid Splash!!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:23.700
Crimson Shadow's effect activates!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:28.830
By detaching one Overlay Unit, Crimson Shadow will not be destroyed by this battle!

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:35.800
I'm not finished yet! Go, Illuminator!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.050
Attack Crimson Shadow!

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.140
Crimson Shadow's effect activates!

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:47.230
By detaching one Overlay Unit, he won't be destroyed by this battle!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.570
Somehow I managed to block it.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.990
<i>Really</i> now? Your Monster just lost all its Overlay Units.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:10.960
Now Sphere Field's effect activates, and all Monsters Special Summoned by its effect will be destroyed!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.210
Yuma!

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.090
That was dangerous...

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:22.800
To summarize, without the Trap, Yuma-<i>kun</i> would have lost!

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:26.930
I'll end my turn with this.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:28.520
Tron...

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.140
Don't quail, Yuma.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.940
Show your 'Bring it to 'Em' to him!

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.480
Sure! Let's go!

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.730
My turn! Draw!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.070
Summon a Number!

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.990
Sure! From my hand, I Overlay Tasukerton and Flelf!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.080
Come forth, Number 34!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.050
Computer Beast Terrabyte!

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.800
Now! Activate the Magic!

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:06.180
Then I activate Xyz Treasure!

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:10.520
With Xyz-Treasure, for every Xyz Monster on the field, I can...

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:12.560
...draw one card!

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.190
There are four Numbers on the field!

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:16.440
This means...

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:22.030
... I can draw four cards!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.030
Yes! It's there!

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:29.040
From my hand, I Overlay Needle Swordsman and Amarylease!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.830
Come forth, Number 17!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.050
Leviath Dragon!

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.600
Then I will Overlay Rai Rider and Zubaba Knight!

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:05.160
It's here, here, here, here!

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:09.080
Come forth, Number 39!

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:19.170
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.590
We're counting on you, Hope!

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.510
Now both of them have three Numbers!

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:32.850
<i>Yuma, good luck.</i>

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:39.400
<i>So, both sides have Summoned three strong Numbers!</i>

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:44.110
<i>Whom will the Goddess of Victory smile upon?</i>

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:47.950
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:52.370
Yuma, the true fight is just starting.

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:53.950
Right, I know!

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.750
I'll show you why you should <i>fear</i> me!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:21:59.920
Quite thoroughly!

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:03.170
Yeah, I couldn't ask for more! Let's do this!

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:15.600
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:21.190
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:31.910
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:36.160
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.460
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:40.170
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:42.790
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:48.010
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:53.350
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:58.980
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:05.440
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:10.950
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:16.200
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:21.790
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:27.050
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:32.550
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:44.400
With our respective Numbers, Tron and I clash hard!

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:47.690
During this showdown, Tron's trump has finally showed up!

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:50.150
And at least, that guy's mask...

00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:52.530
Does that Number have any weakness at all?!

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:56.530
Everyone believes you will return to normal one day!

00:23:56.790 --> 00:23:58.620
Yuma, use the ZeXaL Weapon!

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:00.710
I won't ever give up!

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:03.210
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:07.000
"The Terrifying Duel! Arise, Hero of Bond ZEXAL!"

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:09.210
That's your true face?!

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:12.840
Finally the fight of Numbers has started!

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:16.350
Lots of fantastic Numbers will appear! It's so exciting!

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:17.810
More importantly, Yuma...

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:20.810
Is it true that tonight's dinner is a Number?!

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.440
Uh, I think you mean <i>nanban zuke</i>.

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.730
TL: Nanban zuke = vegetables pickled in Chayenne-Pepper
